(
    title: "Atom Smasher",
    developer: Some("Video Soft"),
    description: Some("An unreleased two-player duel set in the \"Atomic Arena\". On the first screen two astronauts blast atomic particles through shifting doorways while dodging the particles themselves; on the second the fighters cling to the arena walls, sliding up and down to survive the barrage. The prototype even offered a left-handed control scheme and a computer-versus-computer demo mode. Video Soft — the studio of Jerry Lawson, designer of the Fairchild Channel F and a pioneer of the ROM game cartridge — left the market during the 1983–84 industry crash before Atom Smasher shipped."),
